      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-04-02_WidnesExaminer_art0028" n="art0028">
        <head>ANTHONY TRAILL</head>
        <p>ANTHONY TRAILL</p>
        <p>a.ry</p>
        <p>the Marquess of Thifferin and Ava. Anthony Trail has been , associated with Trinity College all his life and for many years has filled the chair of Natural Philosophy. He is an M.D., an M.Ch., and an LL.D. of his College, of which also he has been Senior Fellow for some years. He was born in 1838 and was a well-known athlete in his .younger days, being captain of the cricket XI and for fourteen years racquet champion of Dublin University: and in his later days he has been keen on golf, shooting and fishing. In 1867 he married Catherine, the daughter of Captain Ssewart Moore of Ballydivit, a Waterloo veteran. On the Fry Commission. on Irish Land Acts in 1897-8 he represented the Irish landlords, of which he is one, owning property in three counties. He is chairman of the Isortrush and Giants' Causeway Electric Railway, which was the absolute pioneer of this now popular form of traction.</p>
